{
  "title": "Calorie estimates: powder scoops and shots of hot sauce",
  "description": "Left unknown on purpose when glugs, knobs, shots and ice-cream scoops got weights (nutrition/mod.rs informal_measure_cups). \
Scoops of powders and mixes (\"1 scoop protein powder\", \"1/2 scoop vanilla protein-powder\", \"1 scoop collagen powder\", \"4 scoops Country Time pink lemonade mix\") hold whatever the tub's scoop holds, so a 1/2-cup ice-cream scoop would be wrong; one option is adding \"scoop\" to ESTIMABLE_UNITS so make catalog-fill-weights asks the model per food (a whey scoop is ~30 g by label convention). \"2 to 3 really good shots hot sauce\" (x3: pipeline, Paprika, snapshot) doesn't parse \"really good shots\" as a unit, and a shot of hot sauce is a shake, not the 1 fl oz espresso shot, so parsing it as \"shot\" would charge 3 fl oz; it needs its own reading (maybe a dash) or stays unknown. \
Calories are tiny either way. \
Measure with make ingredient-catalog-audit (Unsupported quantity unit). \
Server-side only (ramekin-core), so no web or iOS change.",
